    "bottomLine": "A strong 240V starter system that grows battery by battery.",
    "description": "The F3800 Plus is the updated version of Anker's large home backup station, and it is the answer if you are specifically shopping for an Anker battery backup. Anker rates it at 3,840Wh of LFP storage and 6,000W of continuous output with 120/240V capability, which covers essentials plus a 240V well pump or dryer circuit. Add BP3800 expansion batteries and Anker states it can grow to 26.9kWh, and two units can be paired for more output. The Plus version increases solar input over the original F3800. For connection to the house, Anker sells the Home Power Panel, and the unit also works with a conventional transfer switch or interlock installed by an electrician. It rolls on wheels but is still a heavy machine, so plan to leave it in the garage or utility room where it can stay plugged in and ready."
